<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antoni Radziwiłł</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–<a href="/years/1833">1833</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Antoni Henryk Radziwiłł</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Antoni Radziwiłł was a Polish-Lithuanian aristocrat, composer and patron of the arts who married Princess Louise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. From 1815 to 1831 he served as the Prussian king's governor of the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poznan">Posen</a>, mediating between the Polish nobility and the Prussian state. A friend of Goethe and Chopin, he composed music for Goethe's Faust.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoni-radziwill.jpg" alt="Antoni Radziwiłł" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Oldermann / After Franz Krüger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_Oldermann_nach_Franz_Kr%C3%BCger_Antoni_Henryk_Radziwi%C5%82%C5%82.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
